      "id": "claim_59fcdf0e99d24014afba1d39590fd7a2",
      "statement": "The MCP server at /mcp accepts three credential kinds, all validated per request: OAuth access tokens from dynamic-registration authorization-code flow with PKCE S256, OAuth access tokens from RFC 8628 device authorization, and scoped API keys (new strap_key_ and compatible existing creed_key_).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/mcp/route.ts#L29-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:239281043d60a01412f5761379d3d21c14686fa69765969319acdb5880380f6f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/oauth.ts",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:fdc129399fea9df4a6d360b408a315c12ec5c5b33c53141e7b93d8b4e3fcde4a"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_352b0e5802b747cfb09c48abf755cd25",
      "statement": "Modern credentials bind exactly one Personal or Company Strap plus a maximum access mode; every call rechecks token/key validity, explicit grant, live membership, and section policy. Modes are ceilings: read-only forbids proposal/direct mutation tools, proposal-only allows proposals where policy permits and removes direct editing, and direct is limited by live Personal policy or Company member/section permissions.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/mcp/route.ts#L2244-L2255",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8026a082965ab032c5300dc5a565c1407a617e2c126952f1d0d904f94151d59e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ad66560698f04869909f5469cc68baad",
      "statement": "If a modern grant becomes inaccessible, resolveMcpState returns an empty state and a missing Strap id is never interpreted as permission to fall back to Personal; only positively identified pre-explicit-grant OAuth tokens retain historical Personal fallback.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/mcp/route.ts#L2444-L2465",
