    {
      "id": "claim_bcb065a3173d4d37aed85d823256ea10",
      "statement": "The authorization-code flow discovers protected-resource and authorization-server metadata, dynamically registers, starts /authorize with PKCE; the user selects exactly one Personal or Company Strap; /authorize/decision revalidates session/client/redirect/membership/selection before issuing a short-lived code; /token atomically claims the code, verifies PKCE/redirect, issues one-hour access and rotating 30-day refresh tokens; /revoke supports revocation. Browser consent records a direct ceiling with no mode picker and relies on live section policy to narrow rights.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/mcp/route.ts#L2338-L2350",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a7cbf3d8aa4c0c8a424f0c8ba75422277a5ad3e06d4c33649620fd1cc35dd6b6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e41eb51a8a314979ab96d45c6a6fff4a",
      "statement": "RFC 8628 device authorization advertises /device/authorize and the device-code grant; a registered client receives a hash-at-rest device code, eight-character user code, /device verification URI, ten-minute lifetime, and five-second initial polling. The user enters the code, verifies the client, chooses one Strap and a mode allowed by scopes; polling handles pending, slow_down, denial, expiry, client mismatch, and one-time consumption. Durable poll timing is serialized in Postgres while local endpoint limits are process-local.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/oauth-device-shared.ts",
